@startuml stack
' GLASKÖRPER vessels demo — DRY tool/format dependency map, SRP design.
' TOOLS float boxless at their natural position in the flow — pink fill
' marks the bespoke surface, plain fill is off-the-shelf. Every pink box
' has exactly ONE output cylinder (Single Responsibility drawn as a
' picture). Cylinders are the file seams between processes: Make is the
' orchestrator, so stages cache and parallelize for free.
' USD was deliberately REMOVED (2026-08-10): with the customer chain
' Blender-free, USD served only the operator's Cycles build — geometry
' files + looks.json are the leaner truth. The interchange door reopens
' the day a second renderer is real, on the same file seams.
title Vessels demo — DRY design: tools, formats, boundaries
caption cylinder = working data, rebuilt on demand (green = customer-owned, gold = operator-owned) · file = authored/irreplaceable truth · pink = our own code (the entire bespoke surface — everything else is off-the-shelf) · solid = runs today · dashed = next in the catalog, slots into the same interfaces\nGPU capability is detected automatically — the same pipeline runs on a laptop or accelerates on server GPUs

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho

actor "patient / customer" as patient
actor "operator / team" as operator

file "web-access-code PDF\nclinic hand-off, the terminal source" as pdf #Honeydew
file "DICOM.zip" as zip #Honeydew
note right of pdf
  the ONLY manual step in the whole
  pipeline: the patient downloads
  their scan from the clinic once.
  Everything after is one command.
end note

file "looks.json\nthe look catalog — ONE source,\nread by scene build and export alike" as looks #Gold

database "DICOM/ — *.dcm per slice" as dcm
database "*.nii.gz — NIfTI-1 volume + affine\n*.json — BIDS sidecar (provenance, on disk)" as nii
database "work/head.nii.gz\nhead mask (dark mode)" as headmask
database "work/seg/brain.nii.gz\nlearned brain mask" as segmask
database "work/vesselness.nii.gz\nFrangi response field" as vesnii
database "work/mask.nii.gz\nthe extraction DECISION\n(threshold + anatomy gate)" as maskcyl
database "work/vessels.ply\nlumen mesh (mm)" as plyv
database "work/brain.ply\nshell mesh (mm, dark mode)" as plyb
database "work/flow.json\nspline threads (mm)" as flowj
database "operator/heuristics-vessels-garbage.png\nextraction QC: vessels or garbage?" as overlay #Gold
database "operator/void.png\nhero still (team-reviewed asset)" as png #Gold
database "operator/scene.blend\ninteractive truth" as blend #Gold
database "work/vessels.glb\npre-compression intermediate" as glbfile
database "customer/vessels.opt.glb\ndraco web+AR model" as optglb #Honeydew

' off-the-shelf specialists
[c3d\nhead mask pipeline] as c3dhead
note as c3dnote
  proven open-source medical imaging
  tool (used in hospitals and research
  for 15+ years) — zero licensing
  cost, replaces code we would
  otherwise write and maintain
end note
c3dnote .. c3dhead

[TotalSegmentator\nlearned brain label] as tseg
note as tsegnote
  AI that recognizes 50+ anatomical
  structures, running on OUR hardware —
  no cloud fees, no patient data leaving
  the machine. Pay-per-use design: its
  cost loads only when a customer tier
  needs it
end note
tsegnote .. tseg

[Blender CLI\nrenders the cached .blend] as rendercli
[gltf-transform via npx\ndraco web GLB] as gtx
note as gtxnote
  industry-standard compression makes
  the 3D model ~10x smaller — fast
  loading on any phone or browser,
  no app install
end note
gtxnote .. gtx

' custom scripts: pink, boxless, ONE output each (SRP)
[frangi_field.py\ntube-likelihood field] as frangi #Pink
note as frangnote
  the core analysis runs anywhere — a
  laptop works; on server-grade GPUs the
  same code runs ~30x faster with zero
  changes. Compute cost scales down to
  near-zero, up to real-time
end note
frangnote .. frangi

[tube_mask.py\nthreshold + anatomy gate] as tmask #Pink
note as tmasknote
  self-upgrading design: when the AI
  tier is active its results are used
  automatically — no reconfiguration,
  no second code path to maintain
end note
tmasknote .. tmask

[lumen_mesh.py] as lmesh #Pink
[shell_mesh.py\n(dark mode)] as smesh #Pink
[flow_threads.py\nskan branch paths] as fthreads #Pink
[overlay_qc.py (nilearn)\nplots the decision itself] as oqc #Pink
note as oqcnote
  automatic quality snapshot for every
  scan: shows exactly what the analysis
  decided, over the original image —
  the evidence behind every render
end note
oqcnote .. oqc

[build_scene.py\ngeometry + looks -> Cycles .blend] as bscene #Pink
note as bscenenote
  automatically uses the best graphics
  hardware available and degrades
  gracefully — the same product runs
  on a workstation or a render farm
end note
bscenenote .. bscene

[export_glb.py (trimesh)\nGLB straight from geometry — NO Blender] as glbexp #Pink
note as glbnote
  the customer chain is Blender-free:
  plain Python geometry + industry
  compression produce the web+AR model.
  Blender stays an operator tool —
  nothing the customer receives
  depends on it
end note
glbnote .. glbexp

' dormant tier: no consumer yet, so no aggregate builds it (YAGNI)
[nifti_to_vdb.py] as vdbconv #Pink
database "work/context.vdb\nOpenVDB sparse fog" as vdb
note as nebulanote
  the next look in the catalog: render the
  raw scan as a luminous nebula — no data
  reduction, scientifically faithful, and
  visually unlike anything competitors
  ship. Activates as ~30 lines in
  build_scene.py; until then this branch
  is dormant — built on demand, shipped
  by nothing.
end note
nebulanote .. vdb

package "customer surface — the product" #Honeydew {
  [<model-viewer> web+AR] as mv
}

package "operator surfaces — team tools, never leave the shop" #AliceBlue {
  [operator review\nimage viewer / pager] as opq
  [Blender GUI\nlive 3D demo rig] as bgui
}
note as opqnote
  internal quality review: what the team
  checks before anything reaches a
  customer (QC overlay, hero still,
  provenance sidecars — plain files,
  any viewer works)
end note
opqnote .. opq

pdf --> zip : manual portal step
zip --> dcm : unzip
dcm --> nii : dcm2niix

nii --> c3dhead
c3dhead --> headmask
nii ==> tseg : AI tier enabled
tseg ==> segmask : brain label\n(one of 50+ structures)

nii --> frangi
frangi --> vesnii
vesnii --> tmask
headmask --> tmask : dark mode
segmask ==> tmask : preferred when present
tmask --> maskcyl
maskcyl --> lmesh
lmesh --> plyv
headmask --> smesh
segmask ==> smesh
smesh --> plyb
maskcyl --> fthreads
fthreads --> flowj
maskcyl --> oqc
nii --> oqc : background
oqc --> overlay

looks --> bscene
looks --> glbexp
plyv --> bscene
plyb --> bscene : dark mode
flowj --> bscene
bscene --> blend
blend --> rendercli
rendercli --> png

plyv --> glbexp
plyb --> glbexp
flowj --> glbexp
glbexp --> glbfile
glbfile --> gtx
gtx --> optglb

vesnii ..> vdbconv : on demand
vdbconv ..> vdb
vdb ..> bscene : nebula shader\n(pending consumer)

blend --> bgui
optglb --> mv
overlay --> opq
png --> opq : hero still reviewed\nbefore sharing

patient --> zip : provides: downloads\ntheir scan once
bgui --> patient : demo: the team shows\nthe organ live, in glass
mv --> patient : sees: their organ in\nany browser or AR —\nTHE deliverable
opq --> operator : reviews QC + hero still
blend --> operator : opens the interactive\nscene when tuning

' layout: customer loop pinned WEST of the pipeline spine, operator flow EAST
patient -[hidden]right-> zip
mv -[hidden]right-> tmask
optglb -[hidden]right-> rendercli
mv -[hidden]right-> bscene
tmask -[hidden]right-> opq
rendercli -[hidden]right-> blend
bscene -[hidden]right-> operator
@enduml
